   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "«Querer que», «gostaria que», «precisar que»",
     "texto": [
      "With a main verb in the present, we use the present subjunctive: **Quero que venhas** (I want you to come), **Preciso que compres o pão** (I need you to buy the bread). With **gostaria**, the imperfect subjunctive is natural: **Gostaria que me ajudasses** (I would like you to help me).",
      "Here it's enough to recognise this common form; its full conjugation is studied later."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Same subject: infinitive",
     "texto": [
      "If the subject is the same, use the infinitive and not the subjunctive: **Quero ir à praia** (I want to go to the beach), not **Quero que vou**. If the subject is different, use **que** + subjunctive: **Quero que tu vás** (I want you to go)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
